    "title": "Describe a noun with a clause",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-relative-clauses-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe a noun with a clause",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Put the describing clause before 的 and the noun. Track whether that noun performs the action or is what the action affects.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "妈妈买的书",
                "pinyin": "māma mǎi de shū",
                "meaning": "the book Mum bought",
                "audio": "9044f04afe7b4ff12b96efcef05cb41d23c6c1816f240193dec5ac3e03a88eda"
              },
              {
                "text": "买书的人",
                "pinyin": "mǎi shū de rén",
                "meaning": "the person who buys books",
                "audio": "c215c6e82e127ab1ec8f29d96ad5345281ee66fedd72f622f1d1740efa17211e"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
